    "accordion_content_YALWAi": {
      "type": "accordion-content",
      "blocks": {
        "item_EeBzkW": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "How do I choose a golf net?",
            "icon": "none",
            "content": "<p>When selecting a golf practice net, consider factors like size, durability, portability, and compatibility with real golf balls. Start by evaluating your space—whether you need an indoor golf net for tight quarters or a golf net for backyard use with ample room. Durability is key, especially for frequent use or high-velocity shots. The Net Return’s nets are built with premium materials and feature a patented design to handle thousands of shots while offering a long lifespan.</p><p>If portability is important, The Net Return’s nets are lightweight and easy to set up or take down. They are also compatible with real golf balls, allowing for realistic practice without compromising safety. With options ranging from mini golf nets for home interiors to larger backyard nets, we have a product to match practically every golfer's needs. Our <a href=\"/pages/support\" title=\"Support\">industry-leading warranty </a>(250,000 shots or three years) provides peace of mind in your investment.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "item_rCbEmz": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Can you use real golf balls with practice nets?",
            "icon": "none",
            "content": "<p>Yes, The Net Return’s golf hitting nets are designed to accommodate real golf balls safely and effectively, regardless of getting a mini net or large net. Unlike many generic practice nets, these nets feature a durable, UV-protected polyester netting capable of withstanding high-speed impacts. This means you can enjoy realistic feedback during your practice sessions.</p><p>On top of that, The Net Return’s golf practice nets include an instant ball return feature, which keeps your practice sessions efficient and focused. Whether you’re working on accuracy, distance, or spin control, using real golf balls with our nets ensures your indoor golf practice mirrors on-course conditions.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "item_FVL9Yj": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Is using a golf net good practice?",
            "icon": "check_mark",
            "content": "<p>Absolutely! Regular practice with a golf net improves your accuracy, consistency, and muscle memory—all critical elements for lowering your scores. A golf practice net allows you to hone your skills without the time and expense of visiting a driving range.</p><p>The Net Return’s backyard nets and indoor golf practice setups are especially effective because they provide immediate feedback. The instant ball return capability keeps you in rhythm, while the net's sturdy design ensures safety and durability. With our nets, you can work on your golf swing year-round and track measurable progress over time.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "item_VmAfam": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Is it easy to learn how to set up a golf net at home?",
            "icon": "check_mark",
            "content": "<p>Yes, The Net Return’s golf nets for home are incredibly easy to assemble, thanks to our Quick Color Connect System. This tool-free setup takes 10 minutes or less, and detailed instructions are provided with each net. In addition, the nets are just as easy to disassemble and store, making them perfect for small spaces. Whether you’re setting up an indoor golf net or a golf net for backyard use, you’ll find the process intuitive and hassle-free. Check out our <a href=\"https://www.thenetreturn.com/pages/setups\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">Setups</span></a> page to see real-life examples of our customers’ golf nets in and around the home. </p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "item_c6XjBR": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Are golf nets worth it?",
            "icon": "none",
            "content": "<p>Yes, golf nets are an excellent investment for golfers of all levels. They offer the convenience of regular practice right at home, saving time and money on trips to the driving range. Over time, a high-quality golf hitting net pays for itself by enabling consistent practice whenever you want.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        }
      },
